    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/feature-staging.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Which site — the repository the change lives in",
      "prov:value": "Learned 2026-10-15: an adaptation repository that declared `site.agentRun`\nwas previewed only on the platform index's site, because the authoring skill\nit followed named the index route alone. Its own site was never built, and\nbuilding it then found two files missing that a copied scaffold would have\nhad ([`sub-kg-lifecycle`](../../../skills/kg/graph-management/sub-kg-lifecycle.md),\nstage 10).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-15"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/feature-staging.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "1. Feature branch → staging deployment",
      "prov:value": "When an agent pushes to a feature branch with an open pull request, drafts\nincluded (owner, 2026-10-31, \"drafts get previews\"),\n`feature-staging.yml` automatically:",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-31"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-31"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/feature-staging.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "1. Feature branch → staging deployment",
      "prov:value": "Waits for the rate-limit window (§7), then deploys to\n   `gh-pages/branches/<branch-slug>/` **only the files that differ from the\n   live site** (`staging-share.ts apply`, owner 2026-10-31). The footer build stamp is\n   filled in the browser on every build, the live site's from `build.json`\n   (folio-assistant#2837), so an unchanged page is byte-identical across\n   deploys\n6.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "folio-assistant#2837",
        "2026-10-31"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-31"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/feature-staging.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "2. The staging banner",
      "prov:value": "**Do not describe it as yellow. It was `#d946ef`, which measured **3.46:1**\nagainst its own white text and so FAILED the 4.5:1 WCAG AA threshold — the\nbanner was not merely glaring, it was the least readable element on every\nstaged page. `#4F6F52` measures 5.63:1. Any replacement gets checked the same\nway; the pale decorator sages (`#9CAF88`, `#87A96B`) all land near 2.5:1.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#87"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/feature-staging.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The facts are fetched, not baked — and that is a storage decision",
      "prov:value": "The banner used to be a bash string in `feature-staging.yml` with the SHA and\na `date -u` timestamp interpolated into all ~530 pages. Because the timestamp\nchanges every run, **every page was unique even across two builds of one\nbranch**: each re-push added ~27.5 MB of permanently new objects to\n`gh-pages`, and the history grew even when the preview count did not. Measured\n2026-09-19 (bean `g196`): 9 previews, **346.1 MB**, and **zero HTML blobs\nshared between any two previews**.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean g196",
        "2026-09-19"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-19"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/feature-staging.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The facts are fetched, not baked — and that is a storage decision",
      "prov:value": "The bash version interpolated the branch name into a string;\n  the client builds nodes."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/feature-staging.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "The facts are fetched, not baked — and that is a storage decision",
      "prov:value": "Those are coupled to the\nlanguage switcher and are `g196`'s remaining half — not fixed here."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/feature-staging.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "3. Commit SHA stamping — and the four fields staging must NOT write",
      "prov:value": "`site-chrome/_includes/footer_custom.html` renders\n`short_sha`, `built_at` and `run_url` into the footer of **every** page. A\nfresh `date -u` per run therefore changed every page on every deploy — the\nsame defect as the old bash banner, one include along, and it **survived the\nbanner fix** because it lives in a Jekyll include rather than in the\nworkflow's injection step. Measured on two deploys of one branch three\nminutes apart, both already shipping the constant banner: 613 files,\n1466 insertions, 1465 deletions, **one insertion and one deletion on every\nHTML page**."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/feature-staging.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "3. Commit SHA stamping — and the four fields staging must NOT write",
      "prov:value": "`staging-banner-constant.test.ts` compares the banner **fragment**, which is\ngenuinely constant; the footer is not in it. This is the paragraph that guards\nthe gap, and bean `g196` records the session that shipped the banner fix, said\nthe pages no longer differed across rebuilds, and was proved wrong by reading\nthe deploy commits on `gh-pages` rather than the code.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean g196"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/feature-staging.md#provenance-10",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "6. The cap — 3 GB of previews in total, the oldest rotated off",
      "prov:value": "**Owner ruling, 2026-10-02 (issue #1868):** *\"cap the maximum number of\npreviews (<= 10) and rotate old ones off.\"* **Amended 2026-10-04: by size, not\ncount, with a budget of 3 GB** — previews had grown to 200–780 MB each, so ten\nof them rotated off within an hour or two. Per-PR cleanup bounds nothing in\ntotal, every preview is a full copy of the site, and `gh-pages` passed GitHub's\n10 GB Pages limit — freezing the live site on 2026-10-01.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#1868",
        "2026-10-02",
        "2026-10-04",
        "2026-10-01"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-01",
        "2026-10-02",
        "2026-10-04"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/feature-staging.md#provenance-11",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "6. The cap — 3 GB of previews in total, the oldest rotated off",
      "prov:value": "It can reach an OPEN PR's preview; that is the ruling, and why the cost is a\n  404 until the author pushes rather than lost work."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/feature-staging.md#provenance-12",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "7. The cone — a preview rebuilds only what a changed file can reach",
      "prov:value": "**Owner ruling, 2026-10-04 (bean `4j86`):** *\"staging rebuild only what is\ndependency cone of changes (general rule)\"*, at FILE level, with each derived\ndirectory's generator declared as `writer`. A general rule across rendered\nkinds, not a fact about IGs.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 4j86",
        "2026-10-04"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-04"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/feature-staging.md#provenance-13",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "7. The cone — a preview rebuilds only what a changed file can reach",
      "prov:value": "A preview missing the pages under review misleads a reviewer; an\n  oversized one costs bytes. Those are not symmetric. - **The old instance-prefix match is a floor."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/feature-staging.md#provenance-14",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "7. The cone — a preview rebuilds only what a changed file can reach",
      "prov:value": "Measured on 2026-10-04: a skill-only change carries no IG; a change to\n`gen-ig-pages.ts` or to the DAK layer's `themes/chrome.json` carries all three. Before the cone, those last two changes dropped every IG from the preview that\nexisted to review them. `staging-cone.test.ts` holds all three as tests.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-04"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-04"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/feature-staging.md#provenance-15",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "8. The rate limit — a preview never cancels the main site's Pages build",
      "prov:value": "**Owner ruling, 2026-10-03 (issues #1868, #1956, bean `j27s`), option 1:**\npush staging previews to `gh-pages` less often. GitHub's `pages build and\ndeployment` keeps only the NEWEST run, so every push cancels the build in\nflight. A build takes about three minutes (2m20s–3m40s, measured 2026-10-03),\nand in busy stretches previews were pushed every one to two minutes — ten\nbuilds cancelled in a row between 07:50Z and 08:00Z that day, the main site's\namong them.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean j27s",
        "#1868",
        "#1956",
        "2026-10-03"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-03"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/feature-staging.md#provenance-16",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "8. The rate limit — a preview never cancels the main site's Pages build",
      "prov:value": "Every waiting preview\n  would pend in one group and each arrival would cancel the last — the\n  2026-09-19 measurement on the `stage` job.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-19"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-19"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/feature-staging.md#provenance-17",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "8. The rate limit — a preview never cancels the main site's Pages build",
      "prov:value": "The `cleanup` and `cleanup-dispatch` jobs do NOT pass through the gate yet. They push once per closed PR rather than once per push, so they are far rarer;\ngating them is the next step if cancellations by cleanup are ever measured."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/feature-staging.md#provenance-18",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "9. Build types — `preview` and `full`",
      "prov:value": "**Owner ruling, 2026-11-01:** *\"preview\" = no reindex, only changes, and\n\"full\".",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-11-01"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-11-01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/feature-staging.md#provenance-19",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "9. Build types — `preview` and `full`",
      "prov:value": "An **index** is computed over the whole corpus: the search index, the LSI\nviewer, the SQLite slices, the handler index, and (owner, Q-CI5-1 \"B\",\n2026-11-01) the glossary pages, the translation status pages and the node-kind\npages. **The cost the owner\naccepted:** a preview of a glossary, translation or node-kind change shows\nmain's copy of those pages, so review such a change on a `full` build\n(dispatch with `build_type: full`) or in its source. Rebuilding an\nindex in a preview shows the reviewer almost nothing and costs minutes, so\n`derive:publish` puts back main's copy from main's writer-cone recording and\nlogs `borrowed <writer>`. The search index was already served from main in a\npreview (§\"Serve the published search index\" in the preview workflow).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-11-01"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-11-01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/feature-staging.md#provenance-20",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "pr",
      "cat-harness:section": "Agent workflow",
      "prov:value": "### Publishing without a runner — `stage-local.ts`, one command (#2410)",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#2410"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/feature-staging.md#provenance-21",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Publishing without a runner — `stage-local.ts`, one command (#2410)",
      "prov:value": "Measured 2026-10-07 on\nsmart-ra: the staging workflow waited **33 min** for a runner to do 45 s of\nwork, and GitHub's Pages deploy then waited **47 min** for about one.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-07"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/feature-staging.md#provenance-22",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Publishing without a runner — `stage-local.ts`, one command (#2410)",
      "prov:value": "Every path refuses an empty build before it deletes anything (bean `oisv`).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean oisv"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/feature-staging.md#provenance-23",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Publishing without a runner — `stage-local.ts`, one command (#2410)",
      "prov:value": "- **An IG repository's own site is built from its AST, not from the\n  Publisher's HTML** (owner, 2026-10-14). The repository declares\n  `site.build` in its `index.config.json` entry (inline — never a\n  `<instance>.config.json`, bean `ymvt`), and that recipe's first step\n  restores the AST from its cache branch and refuses one that is not valid for\n  the commit.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean ymvt",
        "2026-10-14"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-14"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/feature-staging.md#provenance-24",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Publishing without a runner — `stage-local.ts`, one command (#2410)",
      "prov:value": "### Agent-run repositories — the GitHub Actions path is documented, not run (owner, 2026-10-10)",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-10"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/feature-staging.md#provenance-25",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Agent-run repositories — the GitHub Actions path is documented, not run (owner, 2026-10-10)",
      "prov:value": "A repository is **agent-run** when it says so in its own `index.config.json`:\n`\"site\": { \"agentRun\": true }` (owner, 2026-10-14). The first repositories became agent-run on 2026-10-10 (bean `n3h9`).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean n3h9",
        "2026-10-14",
        "2026-10-10"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-10",
        "2026-10-14"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/feature-staging.md#provenance-26",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Agent-run repositories — the GitHub Actions path is documented, not run (owner, 2026-10-10)",
      "prov:value": "**Never dispatch the workflow, to cover a gap or for any other reason. On\n2026-10-10 an agent dispatched an agent-run repository's `staging.yml` on `main` to\nrepublish the root after a re-pin. The site was published, but the run\ncontradicted the repository's agent-run setting, and the owner asked *\"why\ngithub action and not agentic?\"*. Do not reach for the workflow because it is there.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-10"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/feature-staging.md#provenance-27",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Agent-run repositories — the GitHub Actions path is documented, not run (owner, 2026-10-10)",
      "prov:value": "The owner's ruling for now: **skills that drive GitHub Actions are not to be\nimplemented**."
    },
